#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build the embedded Estran tide model from REFMAR observations.

Zero-budget pipeline, Licence Ouverte 2.0:

    REFMAR observations -> QC -> least-squares harmonic fit -> dataset + report

The output is ``tide-model-<year>.<revision>.json`` under
``Packages/EstranCore/Sources/EstranCore/Resources/``. It is decoded by
``TideModel.load(from:)``; the Swift loader is the contract, this script is one
implementation of it.

Data source (verified 2026-10-27):

    GET https://services.data.shom.fr/maregraphie/observation/json/{station}
        ?sources={1|3|4}&dtStart=YYYY-MM-DD&dtEnd=YYYY-MM-DD

    * 4 = validated hourly  -> harmonic fit
    * 3 = validated 10 min  -> extrema cross-check
    * 1 = raw 1 min         -> QC only (not used by the fit)

    The 31-day limit per request is **silent**: a longer range returns HTTP 200
    truncated to ~31 days. Every window is therefore <= 31 days and the last
    timestamp is checked against the requested end.

Usage:

    scripts/tides/refresh                  # full run, writes the dataset
    scripts/tides/refresh --dry-run        # fetch + fit + report, no write
    scripts/tides/refresh --station 190    # one station (debugging)
    scripts/tides/refresh --no-cache       # ignore the local cache

No dependency beyond the Python standard library.
"""

